        <h2 class="section-title">2. The energy neutral street & neighbourhood</h2>
        <div class="body-text" style="margin-top: 20px;">
            <p>Last summer, Stedin, ABB and Enervalis launched the Hoog Dalem 2.0 pilot, with the aim of trading smart energy locally. As a result, locally generated energy is used locally and a positive contribution is made to the entire energy system. Within the pilot, 16 households can generate and sell energy to residents. Households trade their energy via a blockchain, which makes the EWF (Energy Web Foundation) block chain link and creates the transactions.</p>
            <h3 style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 20px;">Acquiring experience</h3>
            <p>With this pilot, the parties respond to the challenges of the energy transition and investigate whether such a local market is a viable alternative to the current netting system. The blockchain technology enables a more efficient exchange of energy between energy consumers and sustainable energy generators. This is a key element of the energy transition, the idea of independence also plays a role: storing the energy and exchanging it with the neighbours. This is the first step towards a more efficient way: from the power station to the end user. The local energy market allows users to communicate with each other and exchange power to distribute and collect energy as efficiently as possible.</p>
        </div>
